cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Tajik Poetry Analyzer"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Schlenstedt
    given-names: Moritz
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-0483-093X"
    city: Leipzig
    country: DE
repository-code: "https://github.com/moschle/tajikpoemanalyzer"
abstract: >-
  Corpus and analysis tool for Tajik poetry, with a focus on free verse
  (shiʿri nou) alongside classical structure. Provides syllable and stanza
  analysis, experimental detection of the sixteen classical ʿarūḍ metres,
  phonetic recognition of qāfiya and radīf, free-verse metrics such as
  enjambment and line-length variation, neologism detection against a
  lexicon of more than 68,000 word forms, thematic analysis and export of a
  derived feature layer. Poem texts themselves are never distributed; only
  derived features identified by hash are shareable.
keywords:
  - Tajik literature
  - Persian poetry
  - free verse
  - computational literary studies
  - corpus linguistics
  - prosody
  - digital humanities
license: MIT
